    "title": "Coachella lineup 2026: What NYC artists are playing this year?",
    "text": "April 10, 2026, 4:25 p.m. ETCoachella, the most sought-after U.S. festival of the year, is here.Tucked into the Coachella Valley in California, thousands of attendees camp out every year to attend the music fest. Some of the biggest stars in music — Beyonce, Lady Gaga and Bad Bunny, to name a few — have all performed Coachella at least once before.Even though the festival takes place across the country, New Yorkers will always find a way.Here are some of the New York City-based artists performing at the music festival this year, and how you can watch.Coachella 2026 lineup from NYCThe StrokesOne of the biggest artists performing this year from New York City is The Strokes.The rock band, formed in New York in the late 90s, has been a fixture in NYC music culture.Several members of the band met in a Manhattan school, and the group performed in some of the most notable clubs in the city to break into the scene. The Strokes are taking the stage Saturday.GeeseGeese, a rock band that has taken the NYC music scene by storm, is also performing. The group originates from Brooklyn and formed while the members were in high school.Geese will be performing at NYC Governor's Ball this year, too. They're expected to take the Coachella stage Saturday.InterpolAnother NYC rock band, Interpol, will be performing on Saturday.The group was first formed in the late 90s, and their music was described by The Guardian as evoking the \"images and moods of New York City, some more explicit than others.\"SombrSombr, real name Shane Boose, will be performing at Coachella this year. The up-and-coming star, who grew up in the Lower East Side, is known for songs like \"canal street\" and \"back to friends.\"He will take the Coachella stage on Saturday.Model/ActrizThe band Model/Actriz, which Rolling Stone described as \"avant-garde,\" is based in Brooklyn, and plans to take the Coachella stage this year.The group will be performing on Sunday.How to watch CoachellaCoachella will be live on YouTube throughout both weekends.Multiple stages can even be streamed at the same time, so you don't miss one performance.A Coachella Livestream app is also available to stream performances and rewatch highlights.Coachella ticketsCoachella is sold out, and tickets have skyrocketed in price on reseller apps.One general admission ticket for weekend one is going for around $4,000 on StubHub as of Friday afternoon.",
